EXT. SALT FLAT - DAWN

White to every horizon. A pickup truck, hood up, sits dead in the middle of nothing. Heat shimmer already.

ANNELIESE VOGT (40s, geologist, sunburned neck, a sun hat tied under her chin) walks a slow circle around the truck, boots crunching crust. JORUND HALVORSEN (50s, driver, gray beard, canvas vest) sits on the tailgate, drinking the last of the water. MOX (19, nickname, nobody uses his real one, shaved head, wide eyes) sits in the cab with the door open. DEV KAPOOR (30s, engineer, glasses, calm) lies under the truck on a flattened cardboard box.

DEV (O.S.)
It's the fuel line. Cracked clean through.

JORUND
Can you fix it?

DEV (O.S.)
With what, Jorund? Gum?

ANNELIESE
I'm looking for the road.

DEV (O.S.)
It's behind us, Anneliese. Forty miles behind us.

ANNELIESE
Forty-one.

MOX
Is it forty or forty-one?

ANNELIESE
Forty-one, Mox. I counted on the odometer.

MOX
Okay. That's good. That's a good number.

Jorund tilts the empty bottle and sets it down. Anneliese lifts her hat, wipes her forehead, and settles it back again.

ANNELIESE
Nobody panic. We have the satellite phone.

JORUND
We have a satellite phone.

ANNELIESE
That's what I said.

JORUND
No. I said, we have a phone. I'm telling you, we have a phone.

A long silence. Dev slides out from under the truck and sits up, wiping his hands on his shirt.

DEV
Is the phone working, Jorund?

JORUND
It has a battery.

DEV
Is the phone working?

JORUND
Hand me the pack, Mox.

Mox passes the pack from the cab. Jorund unzips it. He takes out the satellite phone, dials, holds it to his ear. The others lean in. A beat. His eyes settle on the horizon.

JORUND (CONT'D)
It's ringing.

MOX
Oh, thank God.

ANNELIESE
Put it on speaker.

DEV
(quiet)
Wait for it.

A click. A voice, warm, bored.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Salt Flat Rescue Coordination, this is Marianne.

JORUND
We're stranded. Mile marker forty-one, west of the old road. Four of us. Five. Five of us.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Copy five. Is anyone injured?

ANNELIESE
(to Dev)
Why is everybody smiling?

DEV
Because they're coming.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Sir, your coordinates show you at the mile marker. I can have a team to you by ten. Please stay by the vehicle.

MOX
Ten! That's, that's only a few hours!

ANNELIESE
Mox, sit.

MOX
I'm sitting.

JORUND
Thank you, Marianne. Ten is good.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Sir, one more thing. I'm showing the beacon on your vehicle was triggered at four a.m. last night.

JORUND
We didn't trigger any beacon.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
No, sir. That's what I wanted to ask. Because there are two vehicles at those coordinates.

Jorund lowers the phone. Anneliese straightens. Dev looks up.

DEV
(slowly)
Anneliese, where did you put the second set of keys?

ANNELIESE
What second set?

At the edge of the flat, a mile away, sunlight catches the windshield of a second truck, parked, with its engine running, waiting.

ANNELIESE (CONT'D)
Jorund. Who told you to drive out here?

Jorund looks at the phone. He looks at the truck. He looks at Mox, who does not look back.

JORUND
Mox, put your hands where I can see them.

MOX
Jorund, it isn't what you think.

JORUND
Nobody ever says what it is.

Mox takes one step out of the cab. Anneliese's hat slips off her head and lands in the salt.
